{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4934-1","published":"2026-10-29T10:35:50Z","modified":"2026-10-31T18:00:03.933399977Z","related":["CVE-2025-71183","CVE-2026-72041","CVE-2026-72493","CVE-2026-74578","CVE-2026-74587","CVE-2026-74611","CVE-2026-74624","CVE-2026-80977","CVE-2026-89528","CVE-2026-89669","CVE-2026-89987","CVE-2026-90011","CVE-2026-93787","CVE-2026-97555","CVE-2026-97564","CVE-2026-97945","CVE-2026-98015","CVE-2026-98016","CVE-2026-98130","CVE-2026-98173","CVE-2026-98248","CVE-2026-98253","CVE-2026-98260","CVE-2026-98323","CVE-2026-98357","CVE-2026-98359","CVE-2026-98366","CVE-2026-98432","CVE-2026-99999"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-71183","CVE-2026-72041","CVE-2026-72493","CVE-2026-74578","CVE-2026-74587","CVE-2026-74611","CVE-2026-74624","CVE-2026-80977","CVE-2026-89528","CVE-2026-89669","CVE-2026-89987","CVE-2026-90011","CVE-2026-93787","CVE-2026-97555","CVE-2026-97564","CVE-2026-97945","CVE-2026-98015","CVE-2026-98016","CVE-2026-98130","CVE-2026-98173","CVE-2026-98248","CVE-2026-98253","CVE-2026-98260","CVE-2026-98323","CVE-2026-98357","CVE-2026-98359","CVE-2026-98366","CVE-2026-98432","CVE-2026-99999"],"summary":"Security update for the Linux Kernel","details":"\nThe SUSE Linux Enterprise 15 SP6 kernel was updated to fix various security issues:\n\nThe following security issues were fixed:\n\n- CVE-2025-71183: btrfs: always detect conflicting inodes when logging inode refs (bsc#1257631).\n- CVE-2026-72041: espintcp: use sk_msg_free_partial to fix partial send (bsc#1275510).\n- CVE-2026-72493: net: serialize netif_running() check in enqueue_to_backlog() (bsc#1276951).\n- CVE-2026-74578: crypto: algif_skcipher - force synchronous processing on trees without ctx->state (bsc#1275564).\n- CVE-2026-74587: sctp: fix use-after-free of cached ASCONF chunk (bsc#1277821).\n- CVE-2026-74611: tls: rx: restore msg_iter before TLS 1.3 optimistic retry (bsc#1277804).\n- CVE-2026-74624: netfilter: nf_conntrack: defer invalid log until after unlock (bsc#1277599).\n- CVE-2026-80977: net: skbuff: don't touch shared zerocopy state in skb_tx_error() (bsc#1280259).\n- CVE-2026-89528: svcrdma: Reject Read lists that exceed the page budget (bsc#1280743).\n- CVE-2026-89669: nfsd: fix cpntf publish race in nfs4_init_cp_state (bsc#1280251).\n- CVE-2026-89987: mm/huge_memory: transfer the pmd dirty bit to the folio on zap (bsc#1281819).\n- CVE-2026-90011: scsi: target: iscsi: Reserve a terminator byte for the login payload (bsc#1281280).\n- CVE-2026-93787: smb: client: bound dirent name against end of SMB response in cifs_filldir (bsc#1282932).\n- CVE-2026-97555: smb: client: fix heap overflow in DACL owner/group rewrite (bsc#1283851).\n- CVE-2026-97564: smb: client: reject userspace cifs.idmap descriptions (bsc#1283946).\n- CVE-2026-97945: replace with mainline version and update References (bsc#1283144).\n- CVE-2026-98015: net/mlx5: E-Switch: fix use-after-free in mlx5_eswitch_termtbl_put (bsc#1283963).\n- CVE-2026-98016: net/mlx5e: Fix use-after-free race in sample_restore_put() (bsc#1283894).\n- CVE-2026-98130: sctp: fix a TOCTOU race in SCTP_CMD_TIMER_START (bsc#1283835).\n- CVE-2026-98173: smb: client: fix use-after-free of iface in cifs_try_adding_channels() (bsc#1284415).\n- CVE-2026-98253: RDMA/ucma: Serialize join and leave on copy_to_user failure (bsc#1284790).\n- CVE-2026-98260: exec: Cleanup POSIX timers right after de_thread() (bsc#1284408).\n- CVE-2026-98323: RDMA/siw: Bound fragmented header copies by the remaining length (bsc#1284713).\n- CVE-2026-98357: IB/isert: wait for deferred control PDU completions before releasing the connection (bsc#1284791).\n- CVE-2026-98359: RDMA/core: Reject unregistering netdevs in ib_get_eth_speed (bsc#1284746).\n- CVE-2026-98366: RDMA/rxe: validate access flags before swapping the MR's PD (bsc#1284655).\n- CVE-2026-98432: ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period (bsc#1285685).\n- CVE-2026-99999: ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum (bsc#1285684).\n\nThe following non security issues were fixed:\n\n- Drivers: hv: Avoid infinite retry loop in init_vp_index() (git-fixes).\n- Drivers: hv: Don't reset VMBus connection state on error/exit paths (git-fixes).\n- Drivers: hv: vmbus: fix typo 'substract' in comment (git-fixes).\n- net: mana: reserve RX buffer headroom to fix forwarding performance (git-fixes).\n- netfilter: nfnetlink_queue: unbreak SCTP traffic (bsc#1285684).\n- PCI: hv: Probe vPCI buses asynchronously (git-fixes).\n- PCI: hv: Warn when wait_for_response() waits indefinitely (git-fixes).\n- tools/hv: fix typo 'retrive' in comment (git-fixes).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-default","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-default&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.4.0-150600.23.143.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kernel-default-livepatch":"6.4.0-150600.23.143.1","kernel-default-livepatch-devel":"6.4.0-150600.23.143.1","kernel-livepatch-6_4_0-150600_23_143-default":"1-150600.13.5.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4934-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-livepatch-SLE15-SP6_Update_33","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Live Patching 15 SP6","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/kernel-livepatch-SLE15-SP6_Update_33&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Live%20Patching%2015%20SP6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1-150600.13.5.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"kernel-default-livepatch":"6.4.0-150600.23.143.1","kernel-default-livepatch-devel":"6.4.0-150600.23.143.1","kernel-livepatch-6_4_0-150600_23_143-default":"1-150600.13.5.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4934-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-default","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Availability Extension 15 SP6","purl":"pkg: